# ~/.config/mole/purge_paths — extra roots `mo purge` scans for dev build
# artifacts (node_modules, target, .venv, build, dist, …).
#
# One path per line; `#` comments; `~` is expanded. When this file has entries
# they REPLACE mole's own project discovery (lib/clean/project.sh), so list every
# root you want scanned, not just the new one.
#
# `mo purge --paths` rewrites this file interactively, which is why chezmoi seeds
# it with `create_` and then never touches it again. To re-baseline:
#   cp ~/.config/mole/purge_paths "$(chezmoi source-path ~/.config/mole/purge_paths)"
# See docs/tools/mole.md.

# Main repo checkout root.
~/Documents/Program
# worktrunk / dev-cli park their git worktrees here, and those carry their own
# node_modules / target / .venv copies — the whole reason purge is worth running.
~/Worktrees
